# Studio V3 UI style guide

Before creating or changing Studio UI (renderer HTML/CSS/JS, shared chrome, gates, forms, dialogs, notices):

1. Read and follow [`docs/lugo-studio-v3-style-guide.md`](docs/lugo-studio-v3-style-guide.md).
2. Use semantic CSS custom properties only (`--bg-base`, `--primary`, …). Never hard-code palette hex/rgb in components (including legacy teal `rgb(144, 204, 199)`).
3. Keep `data-palette="default"` / `data-theme` architecture; do not invent a second visual system for loading or error screens.
4. Match form, dialog, button, notice, and gate recipes in the guide (sentence case; Cancel left / Confirm right; one primary per view).
5. Bundle fonts with the app; do not load Inter or JetBrains Mono from a CDN in production.

Embedded match viewer and VS Code chrome are exempt from Studio tokens inside the embed.
